Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 22 06:38:35 2026 +1100

    Tolerate zombie processes in get-stats.py
    
    psutil raises ZombieProcess from cmdline() for a zombie, and the
    process scan in get-stats.py did not catch it, so a single zombie on
    the node aborted the script and the job lost all of performance.json.
    Skip processes whose command line cannot be read.
    
    Prompt: while drafting per-process memory telemetry for devstack's
    performance.json, a local run of get-stats.py crashed on a zombie.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    Change-Id: Ia3033f056e407a950d59d5d52684838d4e9c4d78
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

